- Yeah. So I've worked
with the government too.

00:27:46.750 --> 00:27:48.370
And I would never
suggest, like,

00:27:48.370 --> 00:27:50.530
don't train people because
they'll leave. Like, that's terrible.

00:27:50.530 --> 00:27:52.330
But how do you--

00:27:52.330 --> 00:27:54.445
but how do you think
about the attrition piece

00:27:55.480 --> 00:27:58.390
when you're training people in
some skills that will make them

00:27:58.390 --> 00:28:01.640
able, you know, more able
to leave, possibly for more money?

00:28:01.640 --> 00:28:04.270
How do you think about
supporting them and what you

00:28:04.270 --> 00:28:06.115
can do to keep them
after they're trained up?

00:28:07.516 --> 00:28:10.090
- That's a really good
question. And I'm not a

00:28:10.090 --> 00:28:12.290
manager. So I don't really know

00:28:13.150 --> 00:28:14.470
what they do

00:28:15.250 --> 00:28:17.020
to keep people

00:28:18.210 --> 00:28:18.710
engaged

00:28:19.830 --> 00:28:21.135
